      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-159850",
      ":question/problem": "Let $X_{1}, X_{2}, \u2026, X_{12}$ be I.I.D. random variables with probability density function\n$f(x) = \u03b8x^{- \u03b8 - 1}, x \\ge 1$,\nwhere $\u03b8$ is an unknown parameter. For a particular sample $x_{1}, x_{2}, \u2026, x_{12}$, you're given that\n$\u2211_(i = 1)^(12)\\ln x_{i} \\approx 13.45$.\nThe log-likelihood function of the sample is\n$l(\u03b8) = a\\ln \u03b8 - b(\u03b8 + 1)$.\nWhat is the value of $a + b$, rounded to two decimal places?\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question."
    },
