      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-159851",
      ":question/problem": "Let $X_{1}, X_{2}, X_{3}$ be I.I.D. random variables with probability density function\n$f(x) = \u03b8x^{- \u03b8 - 1}, x \\ge 1$,\nwhere $\u03b8$ is an unknown parameter. The log-likelihood function of the sample $2.0, 3.2, 5.5$ is\n$l(\u03b8) = a\\ln \u03b8 - b(\u03b8 + 1)$.\nWhat is the value of $a + b$, rounded to two decimal places?\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question."
